grid grid-cols-3

When you define grid grid-cols-3, you are creating 3 equal column tracks per row.
  
  ‣ Each row has a total capacity of 3 column slots.
  ‣ Every child element can choose how many slots it occupies using col-span-*.
  ‣ When the total slots in a row reach 3, the next element automatically wraps down to the next row.

Tailwind Class                Meaning in grid-cols-3
col-span-1                    Occupies 1 slot (~33% width of the row)
col-span-2                    Occupies 2 slots (~66% width of the row)
col-span-3 or col-span-full	  Occupies all 3 slots (100% width of the row)

{/* Sample 1 */}
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-5 p-4 bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl border border-white/20 text-white">
  <div className="col-span-1 bg-stone-800/50 p-3 rounded-lg">
    <span className="text-xs text-neutral-950 block">Registry No.</span>
    <span className="">REG-2026-001</span>
  </div>
</div>

